WEBVTT

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:18.950
Rules of the Pretty Boy Detective Club
1. Be pretty. 
2. Be a boy.
3. Be a detective.

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:28.540
"I disapprove of what you say, but I will
defend to the death your right to say it."

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:32.150
So said the French philosopher Voltaire.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.600
After making his opposition clear,

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.520
he declares he has absolutely
no intent to debate,

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:42.690
or even take a seat at the debate table.

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:45.900
A true example of
"do not kill, but do not let live."

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:49.980
My opinion was also
crushed in that manner.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:54.150
No, it wasn't an opinion.
Perhaps I should call it a dream.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:03.190
That's why this is the story of how I,
Mayumi Dojima, gave up on my dream.

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:09.690
But, I'm sure that boy...
that pretty boy, would say this.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:17.150
"Following one's dream is beautiful. But
giving up on it is similarly beautiful."

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:20.770
"However, only when
you give up on it yourself."

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:25.560
Really, that pretty boy says
handsome things, if nothing else.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:30.350
Finally, to Voltaire's perfect maxim,
as arrogant as it may sound,

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:34.400
I would like to add one caveat.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.810
You can't defend anything if you're dead.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:45.450
<i>SPOT THE MISTAKES</i>

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:52.150
I like to look up at the stars at night
from the school rooftop.

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:57.230
But as of tomorrow,
October 10th, my 14th birthday,

00:01:57.230 --> 00:02:02.060
I will never again get to look up
at the night sky like this.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:05.730
Tonight is the last night.

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:08.650
Playing games will stop at
your second year of middle school.

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:12.310
That was the promise I made
to my "dear parents."

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:15.270
Looking for something?

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:20.520
Oh. Crap.

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:25.480
Beautiful.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:34.980
And yet, it was still different
from the starry sky I sought.

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:44.440
Are you okay?

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:49.440
Th-Thank you.

00:02:57.230 --> 00:02:59.770
So you like stargazing?

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:03.150
What makes you think that?

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:06.690
Why, that's quite a simple,
elementary deduction.

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:09.650
After all, I can't think of any other
reason to be on a rooftop alone

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:12.350
at this time of night.

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:14.770
I love stars, too.

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:20.100
Beautifully glimmering stars ever
so beautifully cast light onto me.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:22.980
Looking for something?

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:26.270
What makes you think that?

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:29.100
Why, another elementary deduction.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:32.100
The most elementary
of elementary speculation.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:35.310
Only someone completely absorbed
in searching for something

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:40.730
would fail to notice
my beautiful self standing nearby.

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:45.730
He said that. He totally said that.
"My beautiful self."

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:50.480
I, of all people,
was a bit careless here.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:54.730
I just noticed it.
You have very beautiful eyes.

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:04.020
Why are you hiding those beautiful eyes
behind your spectacles?

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:06.440
A shame to hide such beauty.

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:11.150
No need to worry.
Beauty is not something to compare.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:15.650
Even if you stand next to me, the beauty
of your eyes will never be dulled.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:20.310
That's right. I'm looking for something.

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:22.980
Would you be so kind as to assist me?

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:24.600
Of course!

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:27.900
After all, selfless service to others
is the foundation of beauty!

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:30.520
Come with me.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:32.190
Wh-Where are we going?

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:34.100
That should be obvious!

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:38.230
To the Pretty Boy Detective Club
headquarters, of course!

