00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:34.390
{=19}WHAT'S WITH THAT NICKNAME?

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:34.430
{=19}WHAT'S WITH THAT NICKNAME?

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:39.270
Don't worry about him.
He just went to make arrangements.

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:41.520
Arrangements? For what?

00:14:41.770 --> 00:14:46.400
Come now, Mayumi Dojima.
What on earth are you saying?

00:14:47.940 --> 00:14:51.980
When I say "arrangements," it would
be none other than for a helicopter.

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:55.410
FLIGHT

00:14:55.940 --> 00:15:00.270
And then suddenly,
I was whisked away unwittingly

00:15:00.270 --> 00:15:05.150
to the same beach
I saw that fateful star ten years ago.

00:15:05.600 --> 00:15:07.020
However...

00:15:07.730 --> 00:15:10.400
What kind of middle school kids
ride helicopters?

00:15:10.980 --> 00:15:12.770
Now then, Mayumi Dojima...

00:15:13.060 --> 00:15:16.770
Whereabout is this star
you are looking for?

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:20.980
The exact time you witnessed the star
will do as well.

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:24.980
The trip was to celebrate my birthday,

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:29.440
so I think it was around
this time of the year.

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:33.310
If we find this new star that
Mayumi Dojima is searching for,

00:15:33.310 --> 00:15:35.940
then there will be
one more constellation!

00:15:35.940 --> 00:15:41.150
If you insist, I'll allow you
to name it "Sotoin" after me.

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:46.190
Sotoin, perhaps you're thinking that
more stars means more constellations?

00:15:46.520 --> 00:15:47.310
Doesn't it?

00:15:47.310 --> 00:15:48.310
Of course not!

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:48.460
88 CONSTELLATIONS ACROSS HEAVEN

00:15:48.730 --> 00:15:50.150
Oh, is that so?

00:15:50.810 --> 00:15:55.850
Unfortunately, I am not learned.
What I have is just aestheticism.

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:57.060
A-Aestheticism?

00:15:57.440 --> 00:16:01.060
That's right. I am Manabu
the Aesthete, lover of beauty.

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:02.810
Manabu the Aesthete.

00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:05.560
And there was Hyota the Adonis, too.

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:08.560
And I am Nagahiro the Orator,
he of the beautiful voice.

00:16:08.850 --> 00:16:12.850
Right. I can't stand the thought
of you mistaking us for boys

00:16:12.850 --> 00:16:15.060
who simply look beautiful.

00:16:15.060 --> 00:16:19.310
The true essence of
our beauty lies within.

00:16:19.560 --> 00:16:21.900
He says that, but...

00:16:21.900 --> 00:16:23.980
Aestheticism and beautiful voice aside,

00:16:23.980 --> 00:16:26.600
aren't beautiful legs
only about appearance?

00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:28.600
So if you're pretty and you're a boy,

00:16:28.600 --> 00:16:31.230
that's what makes you the
Pretty Boy Detective Club?

00:16:31.230 --> 00:16:34.770
Oh no, of course that alone
would never do.

00:16:34.770 --> 00:16:36.980
The third rule of
the Pretty Boy Detective Club is...

00:16:37.850 --> 00:16:39.850
"Be a detective."

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:46.600
Mayumi Dojima, you surely remember
which way you faced, the sea or mountains,

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:49.350
when you saw that star?

00:16:51.310 --> 00:16:52.810
Back when I saw it,

00:16:52.810 --> 00:16:57.100
I was playing at the water's edge
like how Mr. Bare-Legs is doing now.

00:16:57.520 --> 00:17:01.310
Excellent, excellent.
Then it's time to set up the telescope.

00:17:01.310 --> 00:17:02.730
I'll help you, Nagahiro!

00:17:03.060 --> 00:17:06.770
Understood. So I'm to be
taking the lead on this, then?

00:17:06.770 --> 00:17:07.980
Hey, you.

00:17:07.980 --> 00:17:09.850
You're going to help me get this ready.

00:17:10.100 --> 00:17:12.850
Don't call me so rudely.
And get what ready?

00:17:13.150 --> 00:17:16.600
The hell do you mean?
You're the one who said it.

00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:19.150
That your family had
a barbeque ten years ago.

00:17:21.400 --> 00:17:26.940
Did I say that? We swam,
we had a barbeque, and enjoyed fireworks.

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:28.400
I said that,

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:33.310
but are they telling me they'll recreate
the camping trip that faithfully?

00:17:33.310 --> 00:17:38.600
That means Mr. Bare-Legs frolicking
like that was part of that recreation?

00:17:40.350 --> 00:17:43.560
Well, well.
You're a surprisingly obedient helper.

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:47.100
I was simply disciplined that
if you don't work, you don't eat.

00:17:49.810 --> 00:17:54.400
W-Wait, don't these have
historical value or something?

00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:57.440
Not really, because he made them himself.

00:17:57.440 --> 00:17:59.270
Huh? Made himself?

00:18:00.270 --> 00:18:05.900
Most of the paintings and sculptures in
the art room are replicas that he created.

00:18:06.400 --> 00:18:08.900
Sosaku the Artiste,
creator of beauty. That's him.

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:11.440
Sosaku the Artiste.

00:18:20.690 --> 00:18:25.690
I didn't know you and
Sakiguchi- <i>senpai</i> were friends, either.

00:18:25.690 --> 00:18:27.850
I never heard any talk like that.

00:18:27.850 --> 00:18:32.440
Huh? Us, friends?
Give me a break. What a joke!

00:18:32.440 --> 00:18:36.150
You must be the type who starts clapping
to the beat but doesn't know when to stop.

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:40.150
We don't talk to each other
when we meet in the halls.

00:18:40.150 --> 00:18:45.440
We agreed to a truce only in the art room
and only under the president's watch.

00:18:46.190 --> 00:18:49.940
Without the president,
we wouldn't function as a group at all.

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:52.560
"We," huh?

00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:57.650
Hey, Fukuroi. Just how
serious are you guys?

00:18:57.650 --> 00:18:59.060
Huh? What do you mean?

00:18:59.690 --> 00:19:04.440
We just met, but you guys have gone
this far to help someone like me.

00:19:04.440 --> 00:19:07.020
So is the Pretty Boy Detective Club
like a hobby

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:08.810
for guys with time
and money to spare?

00:19:10.480 --> 00:19:12.350
For example,
the helicopter and all.

00:19:12.350 --> 00:19:15.730
I feel like you're looking down
on my problems, and honestly,

00:19:15.730 --> 00:19:18.150
I'm not very happy about that.

00:19:18.150 --> 00:19:21.600
It seems like you're a bunch of eccentric,
flashy, and privileged people,

00:19:21.600 --> 00:19:23.600
who are taking advantage of my problems.

00:19:24.270 --> 00:19:29.310
I'm being blunt and saying quite
a mouthful. I'm saying nasty things.

00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:34.980
I don't want to be helped by people who
won't take me seriously. I'm not your toy.

00:19:37.230 --> 00:19:42.850
Nonsense. You've got it all wrong.
Why do you think we're eccentrics?

00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:46.310
We're not playing some
characters, you know?

00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:51.350
Now eat this. Test it for poison.

00:19:57.650 --> 00:19:59.800
"UMAMI UMAMI UMAMI"

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:02.300
"BEAUTY BEAUTY BEAUTY
FLAVOR FLAVOR"

00:20:02.770 --> 00:20:05.150
Hey! Damn you, what the hell!
Don't waste food!

00:20:06.060 --> 00:20:09.480
It tastes so different from
the rubbery meat I usually eat.

00:20:09.480 --> 00:20:11.100
My stomach couldn't handle it.

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:13.400
You don't have to say so yourself.

00:20:14.690 --> 00:20:17.190
Wh-What now? Are you actually crying?

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:20.770
I-I'm not crying.
The juice from the meat got in my eye.

00:20:20.770 --> 00:20:23.520
That's terrible! Are you okay?

00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:26.060
Don't worry about me.

00:20:26.770 --> 00:20:29.440
So embarrassing. More like, so uncool.

00:20:29.440 --> 00:20:31.900
I mean, crying in front of a guy?

00:20:34.230 --> 00:20:37.350
S-So you must be Michiru
the Epicure or something?

00:20:37.350 --> 00:20:41.400
He of the beautiful palate, yeah.
You got it right, so why the laugh?

00:20:42.020 --> 00:20:46.690
Stop talking to me like we're enemies.
I'm on your side. Geez.

00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:50.560
Yeah. Tasty. Good job, me.

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:57.480
What's up? Being cute and thinking, "Eee,
that's an indirect kiss!" or something?

00:20:57.480 --> 00:20:59.190
No, I'm not thinking
anything remotely like that.

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:04.560
It's nothing. I used to live off of food
that I found on the ground.

00:21:04.940 --> 00:21:10.150
So not wanting to waste food is more
important to me than something like that.

00:21:13.400 --> 00:21:15.190
Enough of that already!

00:21:20.730 --> 00:21:24.520
Now, wipe both your mouth and tears,
and look over at that idiot.

00:21:25.150 --> 00:21:27.190
That's what you call a serious idiot.

00:21:27.560 --> 00:21:31.310
He's already forgotten that
this was a case you requested.

00:21:32.650 --> 00:21:35.520
Even if you asked him
to drop the case now,

00:21:34.430 --> 00:21:38.190
Nagahiro, my face is showing up,
and I can't see the stars at all.

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:39.150
he probably won't stop
looking for that lost star.

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:40.150
Leader,
what do you want to see?

00:21:39.150 --> 00:21:43.560
That's his brand of seriousness,
and his aesthetic.

00:21:40.150 --> 00:21:40.900
Stars.

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:41.810
Stars, is it?

00:21:41.810 --> 00:21:42.650
Yes, stars.

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:43.560
You won't be able to see
anything like that.

00:21:43.560 --> 00:21:48.440
If our leader is serious about something,
then we're serious about it. Don't worry.

00:21:48.440 --> 00:21:51.600
No one is looking down on your problems,

00:21:51.600 --> 00:21:55.020
and no one is looking
down on your dreams, either.

00:21:55.020 --> 00:22:01.100
In fact, aren't you the one who's
looking down on your dreams the most?

00:22:18.060 --> 00:22:21.060
Episode 1

00:22:18.060 --> 00:22:21.060
The Dark Star that Shines for You Alone

00:22:18.060 --> 00:22:21.060
Part 1
